tomorrow.

00:11:18.510 --> 00:11:19.712
-But this is different.

00:11:19.712 --> 00:11:22.013
He did 18 interviews
with Bob Woodward.

00:11:22.013 --> 00:11:24.850
-Right.
-He's recorded.

00:11:24.850 --> 00:11:26.852
You hear his voice.

00:11:26.852 --> 00:11:28.554
And you're seeing that and
you're contrasting that

00:11:28.554 --> 00:11:30.289
with what he says to the public.

00:11:30.289 --> 00:11:31.624
Wouldn't that be something
of interest to you

00:11:31.624 --> 00:11:33.458
as a United States senator?

00:11:33.458 --> 00:11:36.928
-Well, let me answer you again.

00:11:36.928 --> 00:11:39.598
These gotcha books
don't really interest me.

00:11:39.598 --> 00:11:41.700
-Uh-oh, someone take
John Kennedy to the shop.

00:11:41.700 --> 00:11:42.968
There's smoke
coming out of his ears.

00:11:42.968 --> 00:11:44.569
We're gonna need to open
this bad boy up

00:11:44.569 --> 00:11:46.005
and check out the wiring.

00:11:46.005 --> 00:11:48.073
And if you're too busy
for gotcha books,

00:11:48.073 --> 00:11:49.642
you should try gotcha books
on tape.

00:11:49.642 --> 00:11:51.243
The president made you one.

00:11:51.243 --> 00:11:53.278
Also, I'm not going to
take advice on reading

00:11:53.278 --> 00:11:55.514
from a guy who sounds like
drunk Huckleberry Hound.

00:11:55.514 --> 00:11:57.416
He sounds like his home address

00:11:57.416 --> 00:11:59.752
definitely contains the word
"yonder."

00:11:59.752 --> 00:12:00.819
with that said, he might not

00:12:00.819 --> 00:12:02.153
have been the one repeating
himself.

00:12:02.153 --> 00:12:04.090
It could have been the bullfrog
stuck in his throat.

00:12:04.090 --> 00:12:06.591
Also, maybe you should be less
concerned about gotcha books

00:12:06.591 --> 00:12:09.328
and more concerned that your
president is so easy to get.

00:12:09.328 --> 00:12:12.231
I mean, he's the dope who agreed
to talk to Bob Woodward,

00:12:12.231 --> 00:12:14.066
of all people, who is famous

00:12:14.066 --> 00:12:15.767
for "gotcha"
on a presidential level.

00:12:15.767 --> 00:12:18.336
Why did Trump think
it wouldn't end like this?

00:12:18.336 --> 00:12:20.372
Are you sure you want to do
these interviews, Mr. President?

00:12:20.372 --> 00:12:21.840
[ As Trump ]
Oh, yeah, Woodward's safe.

00:12:21.840 --> 00:12:23.875
He already used his "gotcha"
on Nixon.

00:12:23.875 --> 00:12:26.411
[ Normal voice ] In the Trump
era, we're constantly bombarded

00:12:26.411 --> 00:12:28.146
with scandal, so everything
feels ephemeral,

00:12:28.146 --> 00:12:30.048
but this -- this should stick.

00:12:30.048 --> 00:12:33.685
You can't dismiss this as some
esoteric DC obsession

00:12:33.685 --> 00:12:35.354
or some insider gossip.

00:12:35.354 --> 00:12:38.924
Nearly 200,000 of our fellow
Americans have died,

00:12:38.924 --> 00:12:39.992
millions more have suffered,

00:12:39.992 --> 00:12:41.527
the president and everyone
around him

00:12:41.527 --> 00:12:42.694
knew that would happen.

00:12:42.694 --> 00:12:44.563
They did nothing.
And they lied about it.

00:12:44.563 --> 00:12:46.966
In a just world,
in a functioning democracy,

00:12:46.966 --> 00:12:48.299
all of these people
would be shamed

00:12:48.299 --> 00:12:50.035
and banished from power
for good.

00:12:50.035 --> 00:12:51.303
At the very least, they should

00:12:51.303 --> 00:12:53.271
lose their jobs in November,
which would be...

00:12:53.271 --> 00:12:55.073
-A beautiful date
to look forward to.

00:12:55.073 --> 00:12:56.642
-This has been "A Closer Look."

00:12:56.642 --> 00:13:00.045 line:0%
♪♪

